				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, a 10-second close shot frames a bathroom mirror covered with thin steam, reflecting a young woman standing in front of the sink while the real back of her head is partially visible at the bottom edge of the frame. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed as she raises her right hand and writes the Chinese characters \"别回头\" on the fogged mirror with her fingertip. The cleared strokes reveal sharp mirror reflection underneath while the surrounding steam slowly beads into droplets. [Shot 2] At 00:05.500, the camera cuts to an extreme close-up of her fingertip finishing the final stroke, with the reflected eye visible through the cleared glass. [Shot 3] At 00:08.000, the camera cuts back to the mirror as she lowers her hand, the text \"别回头\" remains readable, and her reflected face stays aligned with her real body until the 10-second ending.\n\noverall_soundscape: Water drips slowly from the faucet while soft ventilation hum fills the bathroom. Fingertip friction squeaks lightly against the damp mirror, followed by a quiet breath close to the glass.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Very low sustained strings at a slow tempo with a single soft piano note near the final shot.",
